# Constitution: card images and generated output are never committed.
# This file is the safety net; review is the control.

# Source card assets (external — Drive today, object store later).
# Anchored with a leading slash so they match ONLY at the repository root. Unanchored,
# `assets/` also matched src/marchamp/assets/ and silently excluded that whole source
# package from every commit — local tests passed, CI could not import it.
/assets/
/cards/
/card_directory/
*.tif
*.tiff
*.psd

# The one exception, and it is not a hole in the rule above. `tests/fixtures/library/` is
# written by scripts/derive_library_fixture.py, which copies *filenames and folder layout*
# from the real library and generates every image byte itself from a solid fill — it never
# opens a source image. What is committed here is therefore not card art; it is the
# library's awkward naming, which is the thing under test. tests/unit/test_fixtures_carry_no_card_data.py
# is the enforcement (FR-038a); this negation only stops `*.tif`/`*.tiff` from silently
# swallowing the fixture, which is how the whole directory went missing from the first
# attempt at this commit.
!tests/fixtures/library/**/*.tif
!tests/fixtures/library/**/*.tiff

# Generated output and derived renditions (root-anchored, same reason as above)
/out/
/output/
/dist/
/build/
*.pdf
.cache/
.renditions/

# Secrets and credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
service-account*.json
client_secret*.json
token.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Node
node_modules/
.next/
.turbo/
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Claude Code local overrides
.claude/settings.local.json
# Agent worktrees are checkouts of this repository, not content of it. Committing one
# embeds a git repo inside the repo and git only warns about it.
.claude/worktrees/
